    "created_at": "2022-05-11T16:00:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-11T16:03:55Z",
    "body": ">  Starship does something to it when inserting the `$character` so it never works as intended.\r\n\r\nThe starship binary returns the full prompt as a single string of characters. iTerm just can't handle hat case well.\r\n\r\nYou can use a custom module to reposition the iTerm prompt marker, but you'll likely also need a custom top-level `format` containing `${custom.iterm_prompt_marker}`\r\n```toml\r\n[custom.iterm_prompt_marker]\r\nwhen = '[ \"$TERM_PROGRAM\" = \"iTerm.app\" ]'\r\nformat = \"\\u001b\\\\]133;A\\u0007\"\r\nshell = \"sh\"\r\n``` \r\nThere are some open questions around that pr, but #3018 should also fix this.\r\n\r\nI guess upstream could also solve this, the VSCode shell integration handles this better.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/starship/starship/issues/comments/1123964930/reactions",
